The first episode of ''The Flash'' was watched by 4.8 million viewers and had a 1.9 18–49 demographic rating, making it The CW's most watched and highest rated series premiere since ''[[The Vampire Diaries]]'' in 2009.<ref name="S1PremiereRatings" /> Factoring Live + 7 day ratings, the pilot was watched by a total of 6.8 million viewers, becoming The CW's most-watched telecast and the highest-rated premiere among men 18–34 (2.5 rating). It broke the previous record for the most-watched telecast held by the [[America's Next Top Model (cycle 8)|cycle 8 finale of ''America's Next Top Model'']] in 2007 (6.69 million). Additionally, across all platforms, including initiated streams on digital platforms and total unduplicated viewers on-air over two airings the week of October 7, 2014, the premiere was seen more than 13 million times.<ref name="S1PremiereLive7" />

<!--Do not add international ratings for every episode or ratings tables for every country. It clutters the article and we aren't an indiscriminate collection of information. Once episode articles are created, they can be added to the respective episode.-->
The Canadian premiere was watched by 3.11 million viewers, making it the most-watched broadcast that night and the second for that week.<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 21, 2014 |title=Top 30 Programs (October 6–12, 2014) |url=https://assets.numeris.ca/Downloads/October%206-October%2012,%202014%20(National).pdf |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141022153930/https://assets.numeris.ca/Downloads/October%206-October%2012%2C%202014%20%28National%29.pdf |archive-date=October 22, 2014 |access-date=February 20, 2015 |website=Numeris}}</ref> In the United Kingdom, the premiere was the fourth highest-rated broadcast of the week and the eleventh of that month, with 1.53 million viewers.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Weekly Top 30 |url=https://www.barb.co.uk/whats-new/weekly-top-30? |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20101215200025/http://www.barb.co.uk/report/weeklyTopProgrammesOverview |archive-date=December 15, 2010 |access-date=February 20, 2015 |publisher=Broadcasters' Audience Research Board}} Note: The ratings must be searched for.</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Monthly Top 30 |url=https://www.barb.co.uk/whats-new/monthly-top-30? |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150220204506/https://www.barb.co.uk/whats-new/monthly-top-30 |archive-date=February 20, 2015 |access-date=February 20, 2015 |publisher=Broadcasters' Audience Research Board}} Note: The ratings must be searched for.</ref> The timeshifted version got 82,000 viewers.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Weekly Top 10 |url=https://www.barb.co.uk/whats-new/weekly-top-10? |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140718204656/https://www.barb.co.uk/whats-new/weekly-top-10 |archive-date=July 18, 2014 |access-date=February 20, 2015 |publisher=Broadcasters' Audience Research Board}} Note: The ratings must be searched for.</ref> The premiere in Australia was the most-watched broadcast on pay television, with 129,000 viewers tuning in.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Knox |first=David |date=December 4, 2014 |title=Wednesday 3 December 2014 |url=https://www.tvtonight.com.au/2014/12/wednesday-3-december-2014.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150220204907/https://www.tvtonight.com.au/2014/12/wednesday-3-december-2014.html |archive-date=February 20, 2015 |access-date=February 20, 2015 |publisher=TV Tonight}}</ref>

In 2016, according to an analysis from Parrot Analytics, which used ratings data (where available), peer-to-peer sharing, social media chatter, and other factors to estimate viewer demand for various shows, ''The Flash'' was the 5th most popular show in the world with 3.1 million demand expressions per day, behind ''[[Game of Thrones]]'', ''[[The Walking Dead (TV series)|The Walking Dead]]'', ''[[Pretty Little Liars]]'', and ''[[Westworld (TV series)|Westworld]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lubin |first=Gus |date=December 30, 2016 |title=The 20 most popular TV shows of 2016 |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/most-popular-tv-shows-2016-12/#1-hbos-game-of-thrones-with-72-million-demand-expressions-per-day-people-around-the-world-were-desperate-to-learn-the-fate-of-jon-snow-and-watch-the-rise-of-daenerys-targaryen-as-the-epic-adaptation-moved-past-the-novels-into-uncharted-territory-1 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170101002433/https://www.businessinsider.com/most-popular-tv-shows-2016-12/ |archive-date=January 1, 2017 |access-date=January 1, 2017 |website=[[Business Insider]]}}</ref> [[TorrentFreak]] also gauged ''The Flash'' as the fourth most-[[Torrent file|torrented]] television show of 2016.<ref name="thirdfreak">{{Cite web |last=Van der Sar |first=Ernesto |date=December 26, 2016 |title=''Game of Thrones'' Most Torrented TV-Show of 2016 |url=https://torrentfreak.com/game-of-thrones-most-torrented-tv-show-of-2016-161226/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161226175113/https://torrentfreak.com/game-of-thrones-most-torrented-tv-show-of-2016-161226/ |archive-date=December 26, 2016 |access-date=December 30, 2016 |website=[[TorrentFreak]] |publisher=[[TorrentFreak|TF Publishing]]}}</ref>

