The [[review aggregator]] website [[Rotten Tomatoes]] gave the first season a 92% approval rating with an average rating of 7.75/10 based on 63 reviews. The website's consensus reads, "''The Flash'' benefits from its purposefully light atmosphere, making it a superhero show uniquely geared toward genre fans as well as novices."<ref name="S1RT" /> [[Metacritic]], which uses a weighted average, assigned a score of 73 out of 100, based on 27 reviews, indicating "generally favorable reviews".<ref name="S1MC" /> IGN's Eric Goldman and Joshua Yehl praised the show's premise and cast after viewing a press screening copy of the pilot. Goldman and Yehl favorably compared it to ''Arrow'', stating that ''The Flash'' progresses with a confidence that ''Arrow'' did not get until later in the series.<ref name="IGNPilotThoughts" /> Reviews for the series became increasingly positive as the season progressed, with the finale receiving critical acclaim. Noel Murray of [[The A.V. Club]] gave the season a B+ overall, giving praise to the pacing of the plot, the performances of the cast and the special effects, and also pointing out the series' boldness to embrace its comic book influences, something that conventional superhero shows tend not to do.<ref name="AVClubS1">{{Cite web |last=Murray |first=Noel |date=May 19, 2015 |title=The Flash's first season brought the fun back to live-action superheroes |url=https://www.avclub.com/review/flashs-first-season-brought-fun-back-live-action-s-219446 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150612101405/https://www.avclub.com/review/flashs-first-season-brought-fun-back-live-action-s-219446 |archive-date=June 12, 2015 |access-date=June 12, 2015 |publisher=The Onion A.V. Club}}</ref> Weekly episode reviewer Scott Von Doviak gave consistently high ratings to the season and awarded the season finale a perfect A grade, calling the episode "richly satisfying" and also commending the show for "[capturing] the essence of its source material in a fun, light-on-its-feet way that few other comic book adaptations have managed." He also gave high praise to the emotional value and performances of the cast, as well as the cliffhanger and multiple easter eggs found in the episode.<ref name="S1FinaleAVClub">{{Cite web |last=Von Doviak |first=Scott |date=May 19, 2015 |title=The Flash: "Fast Enough" |url=https://www.avclub.com/the-flash-fast-enough-1798183865 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150614214116/https://www.avclub.com/tvclub/flash-fast-enough-219671 |archive-date=June 14, 2015 |access-date=June 12, 2015 |publisher=The Onion A.V. Club}}</ref> The second season of ''The Flash'' scored a [[Metacritic]] rating of 81 out of 100 indicating "universal acclaim".<ref name="S2MC" />

===Accolades===
{{Main|List of awards and nominations received by The Flash|l1=List of awards and nominations received by ''The Flash''}}
''The Flash'' has been nominated for six [[BMI Awards|BMI Film, TV & Visual Media Awards]] (won all),<ref name="BMIAwards" /> two [[Hollywood Professional Association|Hollywood Post Alliance Awards]],<ref name="HPAAwards" /> one [[Hugo Award]],<ref name="HugoAward" /> seventeen [[IGN Awards|''IGN'' Awards]] (winning four),<ref name="IGNAwards" /> ten [[Nickelodeon Kids' Choice Awards|Kids' Choice Awards]],<ref name="KidsChoiceAwards" /> sixteen [[Leo Awards]] (winning five),<ref name="LeoAwards" /> two [[MTV Movie & TV Awards]],<ref name="MTVAwards" /> five [[People's Choice Awards]] (winning one),<ref name="PeoplesChoiceAwards" /> one [[Primetime Emmy Award]],<ref name="EmmyAward" /> twenty-two [[Saturn Awards]] (winning seven),<ref name="SaturnAwards" /> one [[TCA Awards|TCA Award]],<ref name="TCAAward" /> twenty-seven [[Teen Choice Awards]] (winning six),<ref name="TeenChoiceAwards" /> one [[TV Guide Award|''TV Guide'' Award]] (won),<ref name="TVGuideAward" /> and one [[Visual Effects Society Awards|Visual Effects Society Award]].<ref name="VESAward" /> The show also holds the world records for "Most in-demand superhero TV show" and "Most in-demand action and adventure TV show" from the ''[[Guinness World Records]]''.<ref name="WorldRecordSuperhero" /><ref name="WorldRecordActionAdventure" />

In 2016, ''[[Rolling Stone]]'' ranked the show 23rd on its list of the "40 Best Science Fiction TV Shows of All Time".<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Adams |first=Sam |date=May 26, 2016 |title=40 Best Science Fiction TV Shows of All Time |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/tv/lists/40-best-science-fiction-tv-shows-20160526 |url-status=dead |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160527141422/https://www.rollingstone.com/tv/lists/40-best-science-fiction-tv-shows-20160526 |archive-date=May 27, 2016 |access-date=June 2, 2016}}</ref>

==Other media==

===Digital comic===
''The Flash: Season Zero'', written by Kreisberg, [[Brooke Eikmeier]] and Katherine Walczak, with art by [[Phil Hester (comics)|Phil Hester]] and Eric Gapstur, is intended to take place between the pilot episode and episode 2. Kreisberg stated, "Barry will [already] be the Flash, he will have his team, everyone will be in that world, and we'll{{sic}} introducing a new set of villains that we won't be seeing on the TV show. It'll feel like the same heart, humor and spectacle that you get watching ''Flash''." The comic will showcase the entire TV cast, plus new rogues, a group of circus performers who gained super powers as a result of the S.T.A.R. Labs particle accelerator explosion. The group is led by [[Bliss (Starman)|Mr. Bliss]], a character who first appeared in ''[[Starman (DC Comics)#Titles|Starman]]''. The comic launched digitally biweekly on September 8, 2014, with its first physical release featuring a collection of the digital releases, releasing on October 1.<ref name="Comic" />

=== ''The Chronicles of Cisco'' ===
On February 24, 2015, The CW launched a blog account known as ''The Chronicles of Cisco''.<ref>{{Cite tweet |number=570388554607505408 |user=CW_TheFlash |title=Get to know the man, AND the metahumans he takes care of in...The Chronicles of Cisco! |author-link=The CW |date=February 24, 2015}}</ref> The blog, originally based at [[Tumblr]], features posts written by the fictional character of [[Cisco Ramon (Arrowverse)|Cisco Ramon]], at first serving as write-ups of the metahuman villains on the show. Starting with the second season of the show, the posts evolved into the general musings of Ramon and his commentary on the events during and outside of ''The Flash'''s episodes.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Chronicles of Cisco |url=https://chroniclesofcisco.tumblr.com/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180822234428/https://chroniclesofcisco.tumblr.com/ |archive-date=August 22, 2018 |access-date=August 27, 2018 |website=Tumblr}}</ref> On September 17, 2019, ''The Chronicles of Cisco'' moved to [[Instagram]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ramon |first=Cisco |author-link=Cisco Ramon (Arrowverse) |date=September 17, 2019 |title=Okay Fangirls and Fanboys, I have decided, after... |url=https://chroniclesofcisco.tumblr.com/post/187780866486/okay-fangirls-and-fanboys-i-have-decided-after |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200612002035/https://chroniclesofcisco.tumblr.com/post/187780866486/okay-fangirls-and-fanboys-i-have-decided-after |archive-date=June 12, 2020 |access-date=March 16, 2020 |website=The Chronicles of Cisco |publisher=Tumblr}}</ref>

===Promotional shorts===

====''Chronicles of Cisco: Entry 0419''====
On April 19, 2016, a four-episode series of shorts, titled ''Chronicles of Cisco: Entry 0419'', premiered. The series, which was presented by [[AT&T]], features Valdes and [[Britne Oldford]] reprise their role as Cisco Ramon and [[Shawna Baez|Shawna Baez / Peek-a-Boo]], respectively. Set in the second season of the television series, the series sees Cisco attempting to make the Flash suit bulletproof and body-odor proof. While working on these, he receives a late-night Meta-Human Alert within S.T.A.R. Labs,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Siegel |first=Lucas |date=April 19, 2016 |title=The Flash: Chronicles Of Cisco Part 1 Released |url=https://comicbook.com/dc/2016/04/19/the-flash-chronicles-of-cisco-part-1-released/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160420122510/https://comicbook.com/dc/2016/04/19/the-flash-chronicles-of-cisco-part-1-released/ |archive-date=April 20, 2016 |access-date=April 19, 2016 |publisher=[[ComicBook.com]]}}</ref> and learns that Peek-a-Boo triggered the alert.<ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wgC0KrU0Oac |title=The Flash Chronicles of Cisco: Entry 0419 – Part 2 The CW |date=April 26, 2016 |last=The CW Television Network |publisher=YouTube |access-date=April 27, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160505100236/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wgC0KrU0Oac |archive-date=May 5, 2016 |url-status=live}}</ref> She has come to S.T.A.R. Labs to make Cisco create a weapon for her, as he did for [[Lisa Snart (Arrowverse)|Golden Glider]], [[Leonard Snart (Arrowverse)|Captain Cold]], and [[Mick Rory (Arrowverse)|Heat Wave]]. When he does not cooperate, she shoots him.<ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qLsLzvp-dSs |title=The Flash <nowiki> |date=May 3, 2016 |last=The CW Television Network |publisher=YouTube |access-date=May 4, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170606004256/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qLsLzvp-dSs |archive-date=June 6, 2017 |url-status=live |</nowiki> Chronicles of Cisco: Entry 0419 – Part 3 <nowiki> |</nowiki> The CW}}</ref> Cisco survives being shot, realizing that the orange soda he spilled on his shirt was the missing catalyst to his bulletproof formula. Cisco tries to bring Peek-a-Boo back to the pipeline, but she locks him in the cell instead. Cisco is then seen being woken up due to a call from Barry. He believes he dreamt the whole experience, until he finds the bullet that shot him on the ground.<ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JkrW71ysm_w |title=The Flash Chronicles of Cisco: Entry 0419 – Part 4 The CW |date=May 10, 2016 |last=The CW Television Network |publisher=YouTube |access-date=May 11, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160716055039/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JkrW71ysm_w |archive-date=July 16, 2016 |url-status=live}}</ref>

====''Stretched Scenes''====
On November 14, 2017, a three-episode series of shorts, known as "Stretched Scenes", premiered. The series, presented by [[Microsoft Surface]], features Hartley Sawyer, Danielle Panabaker, and Candice Patton as Ralph Dibny, Cailtin Snow, and Iris West respectively. Set during the [[The Flash season 4|show's fourth season]], it shows Dibny as he continually bothers Cailtin and Iris for their help, or for attention. The shorts premiered online as well as during the commercial breaks of the episodes "[[When Harry Met Harry...]]", "[[Therefore I Am (The Flash)|Therefore I Am]]", and "[[Don't Run (The Flash)|Don't Run]]".<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Flash 4x06 Sneak Peek "When Harry Met Harry..." (HD) Season 4 Episode 6 Sneak Peek |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5sQ0WaTrvSY |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190520153321/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5sQ0WaTrvSY&gl=US&hl=en |archive-date=May 20, 2019 |access-date=August 26, 2018 |website=YouTube | date=November 14, 2017 |publisher=TV Promos}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=The Flash 4x07 Sneak Peek #2 "Therefore I Am" (HD) Season 4 Episode 7 Sneak Peek #2 |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y1WNHYWIxA8 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190520153325/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y1WNHYWIxA8&gl=US&hl=en |archive-date=May 20, 2019 |access-date=August 26, 2018 |website=YouTube | date=November 21, 2017 |publisher=TV Promos}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=The Flash 4x09 Sneak Peek "Don't Run" (HD) Season 4 Episode 9 Sneak Peek Mid-Season Finale |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q-EwHPqwcqQ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190520153321/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q-EwHPqwcqQ&gl=US&hl=en |archive-date=May 20, 2019 |access-date=August 26, 2018 |website=YouTube | date=December 5, 2017 |publisher=TV Promos}}</ref>

===Video games===
The series has also been featured in other video games based on DC Comics property. In the mobile version of ''[[Injustice: Gods Among Us]]'', the show's versions of the Flash and Reverse-Flash appear as alternate costumes for the Flash.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Parungo |first=Nicolo |date=October 24, 2015 |title='Injustice' mobile game update adds Reverse Flash, Arkham Knight, Survival Mode and more |url=https://www.ibtimes.com.au/injustice-mobile-game-update-adds-reverse-flash-arkham-knight-survival-mode-more-1477516 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151025131328/https://www.ibtimes.com.au/injustice-mobile-game-update-adds-reverse-flash-arkham-knight-survival-mode-more-1477516 |archive-date=October 25, 2015 |website=International Business Times}}</ref> The show's version of S.T.A.R. Labs also appears as a hidden area in ''[[Lego Dimensions]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |title=LEGO Dimensions CW's The Flash Easter Egg Mini Level (Chapter 5 of Fantastic Beasts) |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W1UJ6KX94bM |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170606004256/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W1UJ6KX94bM |archive-date=June 6, 2017 |access-date=November 18, 2016 |website=Youtube.com| date=November 18, 2016 }}</ref> The video game ''[[Lego DC Super-Villains]]'' features DLC inspired by ''The Flash'' in the "DC Super Heroes: TV Series DLC Character Pack". The DLC pack includes The Flash and Vibe as playable characters.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gutierrez |first=Gerardo |date=October 23, 2018 |title=LEGO DC Super Villains DC TV Series Super Heroes Character Pack |url=https://www.brickstolife.com/lego-dc-super-villains-super-heroes-tv-character-pack-dlc-early-access/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190321023001/https://www.brickstolife.com/lego-dc-super-villains-super-heroes-tv-character-pack-dlc-early-access/ |archive-date=March 21, 2019 |access-date=March 17, 2019 |website=Bricks To Life}}</ref>

===Books===
====Novels====
On November 29, 2016, [[Titan Books]] released ''The Flash: The Haunting of Barry Allen'', a tie-in novelization written by Susan and Clay Griffith, set during the course of the second season, after Barry has closed the temporal anomaly that nearly destroyed Central City. Barry must seek help from Oliver Queen, due to his own abilities beginning to break down, in order to deal with five members of his Rogues Gallery—including [[Hartley Rathaway (Arrowverse)|Pied Piper]], [[Mark Mardon (Arrowverse)|Weather Wizard]], and Peek-a-Boo.<ref>{{Cite book |last1=Griffith |first1=Clay |title=Flash: The Haunting of Barry Allen |last2=Griffith |first2=Susan |date=November 29, 2016 |publisher=[[Titan Books]] |isbn=9781785651410 |pages=1–416}}</ref> The story continued in ''[[Arrow: A Generation of Vipers]]'', released on March 28, 2017.<ref>{{Cite book |last1=Griffith |first1=Clay |title=Arrow - A Generation of Vipers |last2=Griffith |first2=Susan |date=March 2017 |publisher=Titan |isbn=978-1783294855}}</ref> A subsequent novel, following the villain Weather Wizard in his attempts at revenge, was released in May 2018. Written by [[Richard A. Knaak]], it is titled ''The Flash: Climate Changeling''.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Flash: Climate Changeling |url=https://titanbooks.com/the-flash-climate-changeling-8733/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160130122809/https://birthmoviesdeath.com/2014/12/04/tv-review-the-flash-and-arrow-crossover-episodes |archive-date=January 30, 2016 |access-date=January 15, 2018 |publisher=Titan Books}}</ref>

In October 2017, [[Abrams Books]] started a new trilogy of ''The Flash'' novels, written by [[Barry Lyga]], aimed at middle-grade readers in tandem with a similar trilogy of ''Supergirl'' novels.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Serrao |first=Nivea |title=''The Flash'' and ''Supergirl'' to get middle-grade novels |url=https://ew.com/books/2017/05/30/flash-supergirl-middle-grade-novels/ |url-status=live |magazine=Entertainment Weekly |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180824183315/https://ew.com/books/2017/05/30/flash-supergirl-middle-grade-novels/ |archive-date=August 24, 2018 |access-date=August 24, 2018}}</ref> The first, ''The Flash: Hocus Pocus'', was released on October 3, 2017. The novel takes place in an alternate timeline where the show's [[Flashpoint (The Flash episode)|"Flashpoint" event]] never occurred, and The Flash must fight a villain known as Hocus Pocus who can control the minds and actions of people.<ref>{{Cite book |last=Lyga |first=Barry |title=The Flash: Hocus Pocus |date=October 3, 2017 |publisher=Harry N. Abrams |isbn=978-1419728150}}</ref> A sequel, ''The Flash: Johnny Quick'' was released on April 3, 2018,<ref>{{Cite book |last=Lyga |first=Barry |title=The Flash: Johnny Quick |date=April 10, 2018 |publisher=Harry N. Abrams |isbn=978-1419728655}}</ref> as well as a third novel, titled ''The Flash: The Tornado Twins'', on October 2, 2018.<ref>{{Cite book |last=Lyga |first=Barry |title=The Flash: Tornado Twins |date=October 2, 2018 |publisher=Harry N. Abrams |isbn=978-1419731242}}</ref>

====Behind-the-scenes====
On October 21, 2016, "The Art and Making of The Flash" by Abbie Bernstein was released. This is a 160-page behind-the-scenes book with production art and behind-the-scenes photography. The book also includes interviews with the cast and crew from the show.<ref>{{Cite web |title=BirthMoviesDeath: THE ART AND MAKING OF THE FLASH Review |url=https://birthmoviesdeath.com/2016/10/24/the-art-and-making-of-the-flash-review |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170523122658/https://birthmoviesdeath.com/2016/10/24/the-art-and-making-of-the-flash-review |archive-date=May 23, 2017}}</ref>

====Guidebooks====
In May 2018, Titan Books released the first guidebook for ''The Flash'', written by Nick Aires from the perspective of Cisco Ramon. ''S.T.A.R. Labs: Cisco Ramon's Journal'' features "his confidential journal entries, covering everything from his tech designs, the villains and other heroes the team encounter, the team's personal challenges and his own Vibe abilities prior to Flashpoint."<ref>{{Cite book |last=Aires |first=Nick |title=S.T.A.R. Labs: Cisco Ramon's Journal |date=February 2018 |publisher=Titan |isbn=978-1785651274}}</ref>

A second guidebook for ''The Flash'' was released in November 2018, this time published by Abrams Books. ''The Secret Files of Barry Allen: The Ultimate Guide to the Hit TV Show'' features the Flash's "top-secret notes", as well as "classified S.T.A.R. Labs dossiers on everyone in Central City", an episode guide on the first four season of the series, and details on the life of the Flash "in Barry's own words."<ref>{{Cite book |last=Brothers |first=Warner |title=The Secret Files of Barry Allen: The Ultimate Guide to the Hit TV Show (The Flash) |date=November 6, 2018 |publisher=Harry N. Abrams |isbn=978-1419729386}}</ref>

===Audio series===
Audio studio [[Serial Box]] is currently developing an [[audiobook|audio series]] based on ''The Flash'', titled ''The Flash: Rogues''. The series will feature Lex Luthor altering the timeline in order to turn The Flash, Green Arrow, White Canary, and Supergirl evil, while their friends attempt to fix the timeline. The series currently has eight episodes planned.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Baysinger |first=Tim |date=August 28, 2019 |title=CW Shows 'The Flash,' 'Arrow' and 'Supergirl' to Get Audio Series |work=TheWrap |url=https://www.thewrap.com/the-flash-arrow-supergirl-audio-series-serial-box/ |url-status=live |access-date=September 2, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190902125134/https://www.thewrap.com/the-flash-arrow-supergirl-audio-series-serial-box/ |archive-date=September 2, 2019}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=The Flash |url=https://www.serialbox.com/serials/the-flash |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190902125133/https://www.serialbox.com/serials/the-flash |archive-date=September 2, 2019 |access-date=September 2, 2019 |website=www.serialbox.com |language=en}}</ref>

==Arrowverse and the DC multiverse==
{{Main|Arrowverse|l1=Arrowverse}}
In January 2015, The CW president Mark Pedowitz announced the intention to do a ''Flash''/''Arrow'' crossover every season,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Nguyen |first=Hanh |date=January 11, 2015 |title=The CW Renews Supernatural and 7 More — But Where's Beauty and the Beast? |url=https://www.tvguide.com/News/CW-Renewals-Beauty-Beast-1091649.aspx |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170818045347/http://www.tvguide.com/news/cw-renewals-beauty-beast-1091649/ |archive-date=August 18, 2017 |access-date=January 11, 2015 |website=[[TV Guide]]}}</ref> and The CW announced that an animated web-series, ''[[Vixen (web series)|Vixen]]'', featuring the DC heroine [[Vixen (character)|of the same name]] and set in the universe of ''Arrow'' and ''The Flash'', would be debuting on [[CW Seed]] in late 2015.<ref name="Vixen1">{{Cite news |date=January 11, 2015 |title=DC Comics' Vixen Coming To CW Seed |work=KSiteTV |url=https://www.ksitetv.com/vixen/dc-comics-vixen-coming-to-cw-seed/52484 |url-status=live |access-date=January 11, 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150112060742/https://www.ksitetv.com/vixen/dc-comics-vixen-coming-to-cw-seed/52484 |archive-date=January 12, 2015}}</ref> The character is expected to make a live-action appearance on ''Arrow'' and/or ''The Flash'' as well.<ref name="Vixen2">{{Cite news |date=January 11, 2015 |title=The CW's Mark Pedowitz On Expanding Flash-Arrow Universe, 'Dixie's Future, Another 'Supernatural' Spinoff & More |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |url=https://deadline.com/2015/01/flash-arrow-universe-expansion-supernatural-spinoff-hart-dixie-mark-pedowitz-cw-1201347209/ |url-status=live |access-date=January 11, 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150114062718/https://deadline.com/2015/01/flash-arrow-universe-expansion-supernatural-spinoff-hart-dixie-mark-pedowitz-cw-1201347209/ |archive-date=January 14, 2015}}</ref> The next month, it was reported that a spin-off series, which is described as a superhero team-up show, was in discussion by The CW for a possible [[2015–16 United States network television schedule|2015–16]] midseason release. Berlanti and Kreisberg would executive produce alongside Guggenheim and Sarah Schechter. The potential series would be headlined by several recurring characters from both ''Arrow'' and ''The Flash'', with the potential for other ''Arrow''/''Flash'' characters to cross over to the new series as well.<ref name="All1">{{Cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=February 26, 2015 |title=Arrow/Flash Superhero Team-Up Spinoff In Works At CW; Brandon Routh, Victor Garber, Wentworth Miller, Caity Lotz Star |url=https://deadline.com/2015/02/arrow-flash-spin-off-cw-new-superhero-series-1201382466/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150227033833/https://deadline.com/2015/02/arrow-flash-spin-off-cw-new-superhero-series-1201382466/ |archive-date=February 27, 2015 |access-date=February 27, 2015 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=March 16, 2015 |title=Dominic Purcell Joins Arrow/Flash Spinoff |url=https://deadline.com/2015/03/dominic-purcell-cast-arrow-flash-spinoff-heat-wave-cw-1201393858/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150318041408/https://deadline.com/2015/03/dominic-purcell-cast-arrow-flash-spinoff-heat-wave-cw-1201393858/ |archive-date=March 18, 2015 |access-date=March 16, 2015 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> In May 2015, The CW officially picked up the series, titled ''[[Legends of Tomorrow]]''.<ref name="LegendsOfTomorrow">{{Cite web |last=Kondolojy |first=Amanda |date=May 7, 2015 |title='DC's Legends of Tomorrow', 'Crazy Ex-Girlfriend' & 'Cordon' Ordered to Series by The CW |url=https://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/05/07/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-crazy-ex-girlfriend-cordon-ordered-to-series-by-the-cw/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150518082354/https://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/05/07/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-crazy-ex-girlfriend-cordon-ordered-to-series-by-the-cw/ |archive-date=May 18, 2015 |access-date=May 7, 2015 |website=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref>

The second season begins to explore the concept of the multiverse by introducing Earth-2, which features [[doppelgänger]]s of the inhabitants of Earth-1 (the main setting of ''Arrow'', ''The Flash'', and ''Legends of Tomorrow''), along with [[Jay Garrick (Arrowverse)|Jay Garrick]], the Flash of Earth-3, and [[Hunter Zolomon (Arrowverse)|Zoom]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Holmes |first=Adam |date=August 2015 |title=The Flash Will Feature Earth 2 Earlier Than Expected |url=https://www.cinemablend.com/television/Flash-Feature-Earth-2-Earlier-Than-Expected-77097.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160216060518/https://www.cinemablend.com/television/Flash-Feature-Earth-2-Earlier-Than-Expected-77097.html |archive-date=February 16, 2016 |access-date=February 10, 2016 |publisher=[[CinemaBlend]]}}</ref> In the episode "[[Welcome to Earth-2]]", as Barry, Cisco and Harrison Wells of Earth-2 travel to Earth-2, glimpses of the multiverse are seen, including an image of ''[[Supergirl (TV series)|Supergirl]]'' star [[Melissa Benoist]] as [[Kara Danvers|Supergirl]] and an image of [[John Wesley Shipp]] as the Flash from the [[The Flash (1990 TV series)|1990 television series]], implying the two characters and their respective television series exist on alternate Earths to Earth-1;<ref>{{Cite web |last=Couto |first=Anthony |date=February 9, 2016 |title=Surprising DC Superhero Makes Cameo On "The Flash" |url=https://www.cbr.com/surprising-dc-superhero-makes-cameo-on-the-flash/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160212195031/https://www.comicbookresources.com/article/surprising-dc-superhero-makes-cameo-flash |archive-date=February 12, 2016 |access-date=February 9, 2016 |publisher=[[Comic Book Resources]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Couto |first=Anthony |date=February 9, 2016 |title="Flash" Teases DC TV Future, Retro Continuity With Multiple Surprise Cameos |url=https://www.cbr.com/flash-teases-dc-tv-future-retro-continuity-with-multiple-surprise-cameos/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160211090040/https://www.comicbookresources.com/article/flash-teases-dc-tv-future-retro-continuity-with-multiple-surprise-cameos |archive-date=February 11, 2016 |access-date=February 9, 2016 |publisher=[[Comic Book Resources]]}}</ref> ''Supergirl''{{'}}s world is later designated Earth-38 in the Arrowverse multiverse.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Day |first=Carla |date=November 29, 2016 |title='The Flash' Recap: "Invasion!" – The Gang's All Here |url=https://collider.com/the-flash-recap-invasion/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161130190328/https://collider.com/the-flash-recap-invasion/ |archive-date=November 30, 2016 |access-date=November 30, 2016 |publisher=[[Collider (website)|Collider]]}}</ref> Gustin appeared as Barry on the eighteenth episode of ''Supergirl'', "[[Worlds Finest]]", which aired on CBS on March 28, 2016. Intersecting with the events of the eighteenth episode of ''The Flash'', which aired on April 19, 2016, Barry accidentally arrives on Earth-38 and helps Kara battle two of her enemies, [[Silver Banshee]] ([[Italia Ricci]]) and [[Livewire (DC comics)|Livewire]] ([[Brit Morgan]]), before getting Kara's help to return to Earth-1.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Pedersen |first=Erik |date=March 16, 2016 |title=''Supergirl'' & ''The Flash'' Crossover Promo: A Double-DC Tease |url=https://deadline.com/2016/03/supergirl-the-flash-crossover-teaser-melissa-benoist-grant-guston-1201721136/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160319011225/https://deadline.com/2016/03/supergirl-the-flash-crossover-teaser-melissa-benoist-grant-guston-1201721136/ |archive-date=March 19, 2016 |access-date=March 17, 2016 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Abrams |first=Natalie |date=March 18, 2016 |title=On the set: Everything you need to know about the Flash-Supergirl crossover |url=https://www.ew.com/article/2016/03/18/supergirl-flash-crossover-spoilers |url-status=live |magazine=Entertainment Weekly |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160320153150/https://www.ew.com/article/2016/03/18/supergirl-flash-crossover-spoilers |archive-date=March 20, 2016 |access-date=March 20, 2016}}</ref>

